# Workflow language

One setting for the whole app: `localStorage` key `tlc_language`, implemented in `i18n.js`. Order: saved choice, then browser (`vi*` → Vietnamese, `en*` → English), then Vietnamese. Picking EN or VI on any page applies to every workflow.

## Official document title stays Vietnamese

The centered page title is the form name. It does not change when English is on. Do not put `data-i18n` on it, and do not translate it in JavaScript.

- Voucher: `PHIẾU THU/CHI` (or `PHIẾU THU` / `PHIẾU CHI` once the type is known)
- Cash book: `SỔ QUỸ`
- Cash count form: `Bảng kiểm kê quỹ`
- Printed official forms (Mẫu 08a and the same kind of form) stay fully Vietnamese

Breadcrumbs, menus, and section labels are chrome. Those do switch language.

## What switches, matching Voucher

Copy `voucher.html` before inventing a translation. In English that page shows:

- Section heading in title case: `Recent Vouchers`
- Pipeline step labels and the status filter in English: `Approval 1/3`, `All statuses`, `In review (1/3)`
- Form field labels in English

These stay Vietnamese even when English is selected. Do not put `data-i18n` on the visible text:

- Buttons `Làm mới` and `Việc của tôi` (the tooltip may translate)
- Search placeholder, `✕ Xóa lọc`
- Pipeline line `Tiến độ phê duyệt · Toàn công ty` and `· Việc của tôi`
- List counts (`450 phiếu`), `quá hạn`, `(Cập nhật: …)`, and the empty-list sentence
- Status text on a row (`Đang duyệt (1/3)`, `Đã duyệt`)

Other labels, placeholders, and filters that Voucher translates use `data-i18n` (or `data-i18n-placeholder` / `data-i18n-title` / `data-i18n-aria`). Leave the Vietnamese text in the HTML as the fallback. Strings built in JavaScript use `TLCI18n.t(key, fallback)` and must be redrawn from `TLCI18n.onChange`. Heading English is title case: `Recent Cash Counts`, not `Recent cash counts`.

## Do not translate stored values

Status strings written to Sheets and used in comparisons stay Vietnamese (`Chờ duyệt`, `Đang duyệt (1/3)`, `Đã duyệt`). Show them with `TLCI18n.tStatus()` only. The `(1/3)` counter stays. An unknown status is shown unchanged.

Emails stay Vietnamese. They go to the recipient, not the person who clicked English. Sheet names, column headers, and comparison strings are never translated.
